    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What kinds of roles does Jason Obawemimo's experience cover?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "His site reads the same verified record nine ways, each with a one-page resume: AI and Automation (for AI Implementation Specialist, AI Automation Specialist, Workflow Automation Specialist and similar roles); Software and CRM (for Junior Full-Stack Developer, Software Engineer I, Web Developer and similar roles); IT and Systems Support (for IT Support Specialist, IT Technician, Help Desk Technician and similar roles); Operations and Logistics (for Operations Coordinator, Operations Manager, Logistics Coordinator and similar roles); Title and Back Office (for Title Clerk, Bilingual Title Clerk, Title and Registration Specialist and similar roles); Sales and Phones (for Automotive Sales Consultant, Bilingual Sales Consultant, BDC Representative and similar roles); People and Office (for HR Coordinator, People Operations Coordinator, Office Manager and similar roles); Dealer Technology (for Implementation Specialist, Bilingual Implementation Specialist, Dealer Onboarding Specialist and similar roles); Data and Databases (for Data Coordinator, Data Operations Specialist, Database Specialist and similar roles). At Triple J Auto Investment he manages operations across pricing, inventory, vendors, logistics, financing and title processing; hires, trains, schedules and manages the staff, runs payroll and writes the SOPs they follow; supports staff on the CRM, phones and computers, manages accounts and permissions, and administers Microsoft 365 and Google Workspace; takes sales calls and negotiates deals; and prepares and files title and registration paperwork, files title transfers inside the Texas 30-day window, and handles lien payoffs, license plates and temporary tags. He built the dealership's CRM, inbound voice AI and prospecting workflow, and he writes the prompts and call flows for its voice AI agents. He speaks Spanish professionally and proficiently, and he is open to full-time, part-time and contract roles, remote or on site in Houston. The roles listed are the roles each reading is written for, not titles he has held."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is Jason Obawemimo's work history?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Since August 2024 Jason Obawemimo has been the Owner and Operations Lead of Triple J Auto Investment and Rental Operations (https://thetriplejauto.com/) in Houston, Texas. He manages dealership operations across pricing, inventory, vendors, logistics, financing and title processing, and since June 2025 he has personally closed 53 vehicle sales and collected $206,777 in sale proceeds. At Triple J he built the dealership's CRM (Handle a Sale), an inbound voice AI and a prospecting workflow. He is also the founder of Olaceo and of Obavia, live sales-call intelligence for closers, in development."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does Jason Obawemimo build?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Jason Obawemimo builds and ships the CRM, voice AI and automation systems that run Triple J Auto Investment, the Houston dealership he owns and operates. He built the dealership's custom CRM with its Handle a Sale desk (TypeScript, React, Next.js, PostgreSQL, Supabase, Vercel and Edge Functions), deployed an inbound voice AI that books appointments into the CRM (Retell AI, Bland AI and Twilio), and built a prospecting workflow that researches Facebook Marketplace leads (Python, the Claude API and n8n). Together they connect lead intake, calls, scheduling, CRM records and follow-up."
      }
